---
description: Repository conventions for agent edits
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `DECISIONS.md` before changing files. `DECISIONS.md`
records commitments that rule out changes which would otherwise look like
improvements; if a request would violate one, say so rather than implementing
it.

Three constraints most easily broken: never reduce heterogeneous physical
quantities to one number; keep the kernel deterministic (no clocks, unseeded
randomness, order-dependent iteration, or I/O under `src/pdc/` outside
`cli/`); keep units substance-aware (kg P is not kg P₂O₅).

Prefer repo scripts over ad hoc commands. Use `uv run` for Python. Keep edits
small. Cite every physical coefficient. Keep `.context/` as gitignored
workspace-local scratch and promote durable knowledge into tracked docs.
